From 5a7806892303705f13a10b06f63528d6a78c1ae9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:57:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] allwinner: h713: say where a refused system suspend's
 reset ends

Since kernel 0245 Linux writes "STBY" into RTC GP5 at the start of a
standby and takes it back once the display core runs again, so a reset in
between ends in U-Boot's power gate instead of a boot with the lamp on.
The reset BL31 makes when crust does not accept the suspend is one of
them; the comment still said the boot loader finds RUN1. Comment only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
index 4957bc98d..8406112b8 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
+++ b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
@@ -96,7 +96,10 @@ static void sunxi_pwr_domain_suspend(const psci_power_state_t *target_state)
 	 * The whole system: the management processor takes it from here and
 	 * releases this CPU at sunxi_sec_entrypoint when a wake source fires.
 	 * If it cannot be told, sleeping would be a hang with nothing to wake
-	 * us; reset instead, and the boot loader finds RUN1 in GP5.
+	 * us; reset instead. Linux marked the standby in GP5 ("STBY",
+	 * sun50i-h713-mips), so the boot loader waits in its power gate, dark,
+	 * as after a power-off; a kernel without that mark leaves "RUN1" and
+	 * the board boots again.
 	 */
 	if (is_local_state_off(target_state->pwr_domain_state[PLAT_MAX_PWR_LVL]) &&
 	    sunxi_system_suspend_enter() != 0) {
